{%- comment -%}
  Echo one named field off an our_team entry.

  Exists because bracket lookup on a metaobject entry (entry[field_name]) is
  not something I could verify against live data, and a silent nil there would
  produce empty facets that look like a data problem rather than a code one.
  An explicit case statement cannot fail that way.

  Adding a filterable field means adding a `when` here AND adding it to
  facet_fields and the filter_ settings in main-instructors.liquid.

  List fields are joined with commas so they split like a typed list.

  Accepts:
    entry  metaobject entry
    field  string — one of the whens below
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- case field -%}
  {%- when 'certification' -%}{%- assign source = entry.certification -%}
  {%- when 'type' -%}{%- assign source = entry.type -%}
  {%- when 'client_groups' -%}{%- assign source = entry.client_groups -%}
  {%- when 'locations' -%}{%- assign source = entry.locations -%}
  {%- when 'languages' -%}{%- assign source = entry.languages -%}
{%- endcase -%}
{%- if source.type contains 'list.' -%}
  {{- source.value | join: ', ' | strip -}}
{%- else -%}
  {{- source.value | strip -}}
{%- endif -%}
